required_documents:
FOR THE INTERNATIONAL ELIGIBILITY / ENTRY-TEST STAGE (explicitly listed by the department):
- Completed online eligibility form (Google Form) submitted within the 1 January – 31 March window;
- Passport or identity card (uploaded);
- Transcript of the Bachelor's degree, in English (uploaded);
- A valid, regularly monitored email address.

FOR THE ACCESS INTERVIEW (all candidates): all required documentation must be submitted at least one week before the interview date, otherwise the interview link is not sent — 'The link for the interview will be sent only to who give all documentation required one week before the interview.'

FOR NON-EU VISA PRE-ENROLMENT ON UNIVERSITALY (after passing the entry test):
- School/academic documents as foreseen for the pre-admission application, uploaded to the Universitaly portal;
- Where required, a Declaration of Value (Dichiarazione di Valore) for recognition of the foreign qualification in Italy, and legalisation of the original academic qualifications (via the Italian diplomatic authorities / MAECI);
- The pre-enrolment form downloaded from Universitaly after UNISS validation (no separate acceptance letter is issued);
- Italian fiscal code (Codice Fiscale);
- Entry visa for study.

FOR FINAL ENROLMENT AND POST-ARRIVAL:
- Online registration and pre-enrolment on the Esse3 portal after the visa is obtained;
- Payment of fees through PagoPA;
- For the residence permit: Modulo 1, €16 marca da bollo, photocopy of all passport pages, UNISS validation of the study period length, health insurance copy, €30.46 payment slip, accommodation contract, fiscal code.

NOT REQUIRED / NOT MENTIONED: the official IMAST pages do NOT list a motivation letter, reference/recommendation letters or a CV as compulsory documents for IMAST (a motivational interview is required for the department's separate Master in Economics, in Italian, not for IMAST). An English language certificate is not compulsory but, where held, exempts the candidate from the English assessment. [uncertain: whether a CV or motivation letter is requested informally at the interview stage — not listed on official pages]
